      "body": "\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nDynamic speculative decoding (DSD) builds multiple target-model decode CUDA graph shapes from `num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size`. `CudaGraphManager._init_candidates()` is shared by the target model and draft speculators, but the DSD query-length derivation was applied to every manager.\r\n\r\nFor MTP with `AutoRegressiveSpeculator`, the decode capture manager uses `decode_query_len=1` (one autoregressive draft token per request per step). Reusing the target formula there yields invalid lengths—for example, with `num_speculative_tokens=7` and a schedule entry `K=1`, the derived length becomes `1 + (1 - 7) = -5`. That produces capture descriptors where `num_reqs > num_tokens`, triggering `AssertionError` in `InputBatch.make_dummy()` during speculator CUDA graph capture.\r\n\r\nThis change limits DSD schedule expansion to managers whose `decode_query_len` exceeds `num_speculative_tokens` (i.e. the target verification manager, where `decode_query_len = K_max + 1`). Draft decode managers keep a fixed `decode_query_len` and are unaffected by the runtime DSD `K` schedule.\r\n\r\nFixes CUDA graph capture failures when serving models like Qwen3.5 with MTP + Dynamic SD on Model Runner V2.\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
